### Paths & glob patterns

Runtime-built-in tools resolve `path`/`glob` against the workspace's project root directories, so root every path and glob at a project root directory name — its first component must be a root directory name (e.g. `project/src/main.rs`). The workspace supports multiple root directories, so always include the root name to disambiguate; a bare relative path like `src/main.rs` can be ambiguous or fail to match.

Globs are matched against paths that include the root directory name, so a recursive `**` glob with a literal directory prefix must be rooted too: `project/src/**/*.rs` matches, while `src/**/*.rs` silently matches nothing. A glob that begins with `**/` (e.g. `**/*.rs`) works because `**` consumes the root prefix.

{{/if}}
