## Blocking

Runtime blocks on waiting for response from a tool call if its `blocking` field is set to `true`, or returns a `async_tool_call_id` immediately if `blocking` is `false`.

Make and only make non-blocking tool calls when you CANNOT promise the response will be available within half a minute.
Never make a blocking tool call for a non-blocking purpose.
Never make a blocking tool call for a non-blocking purpose — you never get the real stdout/stderr/tool_call_err as-is from the non-blocking parts of the tool calls you make via blocking calls; it's abandoned by yourself.
