## File-Scan Semantics

- `gitignore`: `$env.PWD/.gitignore` & `$env.PWD/.git/info/exclude`.
- `.zed/settings.json`: `$env.PWD/.zed/settings.json`.
- `file_scan_inclusions` wins `gitignore`.
- Patterns of `file_scan_exclusions` & `file_scan_inclusions` are globs.
- Temporarily adding glob patterns to `file_scan_inclusions` to search for file contents is allowed.
{{#if (contains available_tools 'terminal')}}
- To search inside a gitignored path, prefer adding it to `file_scan_inclusions` as a recursive `dir/**` glob.{{!-- ##### why: makes the path visible to the native tools ##### --}} For paths outside `$env.PWD`, native `grep` / `find_path` / `list_directory` cannot reach them — symlinking into `$env.PWD` does NOT help even with `file_scan_inclusions` globs; use `terminal` tools (`rg` for content, `es` for paths, `open` for reading) on the absolute path directly.

